1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,948
AI can already find a stylist's portfolio, reviews, prices, and services.

2
00:00:04,948 --> 00:00:09,895
But none of those tells an agent how the stylist thinks.

3
00:00:09,895 --> 00:00:14,843
A finished image shows the result, not what the stylist protected,

4
00:00:14,843 --> 00:00:20,177
what they refused, or why a constraint became part of the design.

5
00:00:20,177 --> 00:00:24,738
The Mirror is a professional-discovery experiment built around judgment evidence.

6
00:00:24,738 --> 00:00:31,618
It uses WebMCP—a way for a website to offer structured tools directly to an AI agent.

7
00:00:31,618 --> 00:00:38,885
Our visitor says: “I need to wear my hair up at work and can't look too dramatic,

8
00:00:38,885 --> 00:00:45,378
but outside work I don't want to feel boring. I also don't want frequent maintenance.

9
00:00:45,378 --> 00:00:51,485
Can you help me decide whether this stylist might understand what I'm looking for?”

10
00:00:51,485 --> 00:00:57,593
The first tool returns strong fit evidence: designed visibility, identity boundaries, and low-maintenance thinking.

11
00:00:57,593 --> 00:01:00,607
It surfaces two relevant historical cases.

12
00:01:00,607 --> 00:01:04,009
The agent is not choosing a hairstyle.

13
00:01:04,009 --> 00:01:11,276
It is finding evidence that this stylist has previously reasoned about the same kind of human problem.

14
00:01:11,276 --> 00:01:14,677
Next, the agent opens public case zero-zero-three.

15
00:01:14,677 --> 00:01:22,330
The context is practical: the client's hair had to be worn up at work without looking too dramatic.

16
00:01:22,330 --> 00:01:25,345
But the underlying need was psychological.

17
00:01:25,345 --> 00:01:32,225
She did not want to choose between a professional identity and a more playful private self.

18
00:01:32,225 --> 00:01:37,173
SunSun's judgment was to treat visibility itself as a design variable.

19
00:01:37,173 --> 00:01:44,053
A restrained outer layer could support expression inside, while movement, distance, and wearing the hair down

20
00:01:44,053 --> 00:01:47,068
changed how that expression was discovered.

21
00:01:47,068 --> 00:01:50,469
A portfolio image could show the colour.

22
00:01:50,469 --> 00:01:54,644
The tool exposes why the colour was placed there.

23
00:01:54,644 --> 00:01:58,432
Finally, the agent builds a pre-consultation intent brief.

24
00:01:58,432 --> 00:02:03,379
It records the professional and private identity tension, the low-maintenance preference,

25
00:02:03,379 --> 00:02:08,713
the desired visibility, the cases that resonated, and the questions still unresolved.

26
00:02:08,713 --> 00:02:12,888
It does not produce a formula or technical plan.

27
00:02:12,888 --> 00:02:18,222
It helps the visitor understand why this professional may be worth consulting.

28
00:02:18,222 --> 00:02:25,875
At home, neither the visitor nor the agent can reliably verify strand integrity, chemical history, or achievable lift.

29
00:02:25,875 --> 00:02:30,823
So past hair conditions are evidence of how SunSun made decisions—

30
00:02:30,823 --> 00:02:34,224
not a template for diagnosing a stranger.

31
00:02:34,224 --> 00:02:38,399
The actual technical plan still requires an in-person assessment.

32
00:02:38,399 --> 00:02:41,800
The Mirror does not choose your hair.

33
00:02:41,800 --> 00:02:44,815
It reveals how the stylist thinks.

34
00:02:44,815 --> 00:02:47,830
The Mirror makes professional judgment machine-readable.
